## Resolved mutable: deployed-no-world-until-refresh-rootcause

WITNESSED live https://anentrypoint.github.io/spoint/demo.html?singleplayer&world=tps-game (browser-7/8 + deployed-firstload.png): the WORLD IS FULLY LOADED on first load (98 meshes all visible, env-sillos present+visible, FPS 61-106) but the LOADING SCREEN stayed display:block COVERING it (browser-8 loadingDisplay=block). Root cause = checkAllLoaded (app.js:69) gates loadingScreen.hide() on a 5-condition boolean conjunction (assetsLoaded && environmentLoaded && firstSnapshotReceived && modelsPrefetched && firstSnapshotEntityPending.size===0) with NO timeout/fallback. environmentLoaded flips only inside onFirstEntityLoaded (app.js:68) which fires on the first entity mesh load; firstSnapshotEntityPending entries (added from snapshot e.model entities, app.js:133) must each fire onFirstEntityLoaded to be deleted. When a ModelPool-routed/streamed entity loads without firing onMeshReady/onFirstEntityLoaded (the documented ModelPool engagement race), a flag never flips -> the gate never completes -> loading screen never hides -> world is loaded but obscured, until a refresh warms the cache and the timing resolves. Compounded by the dark .app/body bg (rgb19,19,24) on the old deployed build (no canvas-host). FIX: replace the fragile boolean gate with an xstate loading machine tracking every step + a fallback timeout that forces ready so a missed callback can never trap the loading screen. (Deployed build is OLD: window.__app.clientMachine undefined, browser-7 machine=no.)